    },
    {
      "turn": 1,
      "book_revision": 1,
      "note": "Tone = grounded near-future noir. Setting = New Halcyon (vertical: docks/margins -> corporate spires). Names locked: PC = WREN (codename) / 'Vesper' (buried true name); father = Dr. Elias Marrow; rogue = Cain; company = Vance Dynamics; villain = The Chairman/Aldous Vance; handler = 'Sloane' (TBC). Player = fixed identity (NOT player-named, protects the Wren/Vesper reveal). Systems = phone YES, clothing YES (disguise+seduction), money YES (reframed as upgrade economy, NO landlord rent), customization minimal/NO creator."
    },
    {
      "turn": 1,
      "book_revision": 1,
      "note": "PHASE 1 boundary locked: cold status-quo + first crack. Opens mid-honeypot (teaches the loop + advances the hunt) -> handler assigns the kill-the-rogue mission -> memory-leaks begin -> chase Cain to a just-vacated strike site -> recover details + a badly damaged memory chip -> analysis = first undeniable leak ('I had a life before them'). Phase 1 ENDS there; first secret move against the company opens Phase 2."
    },
    {
      "turn": 1,
      "book_revision": 1,
      "note": "Working-process note: LO prefers concrete pitches he can react to/edit over AskUserQuestion multiple-choice forks (rejected the tool 3x this session, each time to clarify/discuss). Lead with honest opinion + concrete options in prose."
    },
    {
      "turn": 2,
      "book_revision": 2,
      "note": "NATURE REVISION: she is HALF-HUMAN, not a pure machine. Marrow's breakthrough = human-derived beings (that's why they truly feel); Cain is half-human too. Her human memory is wiped ('whose human' stays buried, feeds the central reveal, never a forked subplot). THE LEAK: her body enjoys sex from the start and she doesn't know why = the one human thing the company couldn't suppress = a scene-one tell. DISCIPLINE: sensation NOT emotion (emotional thaw still reserved for the kill-or-love ending); never let bodily pleasure become a want she acts on (keeps surrender intact). Chairman SHARPENED: he wants to become a human-machine fusion (immortality WITH a feeling self); the half-human secret is exactly what he kills to get; she's the working prototype."
