      "turn": 2,
      "book_revision": 2,
      "note": "THE GAME-LAYER FIX (diagnosis: we'd designed a passive STORY, not a GAME — no player want/agency/loop). FIX: (1) player's driving want = HUNT THE 'EVIL' ROGUE — one clear mission; the 'evil' is the company's LIE so the want INVERTS at the reveal (kill -> love), wired to the ending. (2) Structure = an OPEN WEB of conquerable powerful men (not a line): each mark = conquest + clue + resources + sometimes a wrong-note; player chooses which thread/order = the agency. Engine-native (zones+NPCs+flags). (3) Two layers of want: directional (catch him) + visceral (own these men). (4) Capability DEMOTED to enabler (reach harder marks), not the want; body-upgrades mostly Act-2. KILLED the Integration/feeling meter. Chip = mystery recovered in pieces, not a humanity bar."
